      dealing: "Each player shuffles the other's pack. Each deals from own pack: 12 face-down + 1 face-up (reserve), 4 face-up in a column above reserve (houses). Thirty-five cards remain as hand. Space between tableau columns for eight foundation piles.",
    },
    turnFlow: "1. Setup: Each player shuffles the other's pack; each deals 12 face-down and one face-up (reserve), 4 face-up tableau cards (houses), and holds 35 cards (hand). Space between columns for eight foundation piles.\n2. First player: Lower top reserve card (K high, A low) starts; if equal, compare house cards.\n3. Turn: Play available cards (reserve top, tableau outermost, then hand card when no compulsory moves)—to foundations (Ace then same-suit ascending), tableau (descending alternating color), or load onto opponent's reserve/waste (same suit, rank ±1). Compulsory: reserve to foundation first; any available to foundation; fill empty tableau from reserve before turning hand card. Opponent may call Stop on violation; undo move and opponent plays.\n4. End: First with no hand, reserve, or waste wins. Stalemate: lower remaining count wins (hand/waste 1 each, reserve 2 each).",
