    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 5 card(s) per player.',
      "Rule example: Be the first player to get rid of all cards from your hand, waste pile, and reserve by playing them to the eight foundations (Ace to King same suit), the eight tableau houses (descending alternating colors), or by loading onto the opponent's reserve or waste (same suit, adjacent rank). Opponent may call Stop on an illegal or omitted compulsory move.",
      "Turn-flow example: 1. Setup: Each player shuffles the other's pack; each deals 12 face-down and one face-up (reserve), 4 face-up tableau cards (houses), and holds 35 cards (hand). Space between columns for eight foundation piles.\n2. First player: Lower top reserve card (K high, A low) starts; if equal, compare house cards.\n3. Turn: Play available cards (reserve top, tableau outermost, then hand card when no compulsory moves)—to foundations (Ace then same-suit ascending), tableau (descending alternating color), or load onto opponent's reserve/waste (same suit, rank ±1). Compulsory: reserve to foundation first; any available to foundation; fill empty tableau from reserve before turning hand card. Opponent may call Stop on violation; undo move and opponent plays.\n4. End: First with no hand, reserve, or waste wins. Stalemate: lower remaining count wins (hand/waste 1 each, reserve 2 each).",
      "Scoring example: Winner scores 30 points plus 1 per card left in opponent's hand and waste piles, plus 2 per card left in opponent's reserve. Stalemate: player with lower remaining count scores the difference (no 30-point bonus). Agreed target (e.g. 300) wins the match. First player to play off all cards from hand, reserve, and waste pile wins the game; first to reach agreed target score (e.g. 300) wins the match..",
